    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="18">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ger">Ger</ref> 18</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="455" ed="#liebermann"/>Hit is earfoðe eall to gesecganne, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> se beðencan sceal, ðe scire healt.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#gobbitt" n="30" corresp="#wit-b">Hit is earfoðe eall to gesecganne þæt se beðen|can sceal ðe scire healt .</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="338" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Hit is earfoðe eall to gesecganne þæt se beðencan sceal ðe scire healt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="455" ed="#liebermann"/>Es ist schwierig, alles zu sagen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="g" target="#Ger_18.lnote.de1.g"/>, was der bedenken muss, welcher das [Gutsverwalter-]Amt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="o" target="#Ger_18.lnote.de1.o"/> innehat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">It is difficult to tell all that he must think of who holds the [reeve's] office.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">It is difficult to say everything that one who runs a shire must keep in mind;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="339" ed="#rabin-doml"/>It is difficult to recount all that that must be remembered by the person who oversees a shire.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">1. Zupitza emends ‘forða’ to ‘forðam’, but ‘forðe’ occurs for ‘vor’ in the 12th century. B's ‘mehte’ (e for æ) and ‘hæpsan’ stand so. Liebermann compares Gerefa 2, 4, 12 and 17.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ger_18.lnote.de1.g" n="g" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">455</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 12; <hi rend="italic">u.</hi> 17 <hi rend="italic">f.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 12; <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 17 <hi rend="italic">f.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ger_18.lnote.de1.o" n="o" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">455</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 2</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
